WEBVTT

00:00:30.924 --> 00:00:34.691
I can't believe we
actually bought this thing.

00:00:34.724 --> 00:00:37.324
There's a reason charity
auctions have an open bar.

00:00:37.357 --> 00:00:39.257
Don't you think...

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.390
I don't know, it's kind of creepy?

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:45.457
It's okay.

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:47.958
I'll keep you safe.

00:00:49.058 --> 00:00:51.390
Maybe you're the one i
ought to be scared of.

00:00:53.457 --> 00:00:56.557
Mmm. Let's go upstairs.

00:00:56.591 --> 00:00:59.691
Give me 10 minutes to lock up.

00:00:59.724 --> 00:01:01.591
Mmm.

00:01:01.624 --> 00:01:03.123
Make than one minute.

00:01:52.657 --> 00:01:55.958
If you don't hurry up, i'm
gonna start without you!

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:18.891
Babe, get the lights.
I can't see a thing.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.857
Do you smell something?

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:29.991
Ann?

00:02:32.657 --> 00:02:34.190
Ann?!

00:02:52.757 --> 00:02:55.357

...3-4-2-0.

00:02:56.424 --> 00:02:58.490
All right. You're in there.

00:02:58.524 --> 00:02:59.624
Perfect.

00:02:59.657 --> 00:03:02.390
So, is that brandi with a "y" or an "i"?

00:03:19.891 --> 00:03:22.924
All right, listen. I got to go.

00:03:22.958 --> 00:03:25.058
Hold that thought. I'll
be right back, okay?

00:03:27.123 --> 00:03:29.757
All right, so, i think i got
something. Oh, yeah, me too.

00:03:29.791 --> 00:03:31.724
I think we need to take
a little shore leave

00:03:31.757 --> 00:03:33.791
For just a little bit.
What do you think, huh?

00:03:33.824 --> 00:03:35.457
I'm so in the door with this one here.

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:37.891
So, what are we today,
dean? Are we rock stars?

00:03:37.924 --> 00:03:39.223
Are we army rangers?

00:03:39.257 --> 00:03:41.924
We're l.A. Tv scouts looking
for people with special skills.

00:03:43.024 --> 00:03:45.058
But, hey, it's not that far off, right?

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:47.791
By the way, she's got
a friend over there.

00:03:47.824 --> 00:03:49.657
I can probably hook you
up. What do you think?

00:03:49.691 --> 00:03:51.424
Dean, uh, no thanks.
I can get my own dates.

00:03:51.457 --> 00:03:53.524
Yeah, you can, but you don't.

00:03:53.557 --> 00:03:55.591
What is that supposed to mean?

00:03:55.624 --> 00:03:57.324
Nothing. What do you got?

00:03:57.357 --> 00:03:59.891
Mark and ann telesca
of new paltz, new york,

00:03:59.924 --> 00:04:02.991
Were both found dead in their
home just a few days ago.

00:04:03.024 --> 00:04:04.857
Throats were slit, there were no prints,

00:04:04.891 --> 00:04:06.657
No murder weapons, all
- Dean?

00:04:06.691 --> 00:04:07.958
No prints, no murder weapons,

00:04:07.991 --> 00:04:09.958
All doors and windows were
locked from the inside.

00:04:09.991 --> 00:04:12.058
Could just be a garden-Variety murder.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.390
You know, not our department.
No, dad says different.

00:04:14.424 --> 00:04:15.457
What do you mean?

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:16.457
Look.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:17.657
Dad noted three murders

00:04:17.691 --> 00:04:19.591
In the same area of upstate new york.

00:04:19.624 --> 00:04:22.157
First one, right here, 1912.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:25.958
The second one in 1945,
and the third in 1970.

00:04:25.991 --> 00:04:28.524
The same m.O. As the telescas
- The throats were slit,

00:04:28.557 --> 00:04:30.324
The houses were locked from the inside.

00:04:30.357 --> 00:04:31.891
So much time passed between the murders

00:04:31.924 --> 00:04:33.724
That nobody checked the
pattern except for dad.

00:04:33.757 --> 00:04:35.757
He always kept his eyes
peeled for another one.

00:04:35.791 --> 00:04:37.123
And now we got one. Exactly.

00:04:37.157 --> 00:04:39.357
All right. I'm with you.
It's worth checking out.

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:41.624
We can't pick this up till
first thing, though, right?

00:04:41.657 --> 00:04:43.958
Yeah. Good.

00:04:43.991 --> 00:04:45.457
Dean...

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:46.924
Ladies. Did you miss me?

00:04:46.958 --> 00:04:48.624
I'm just kidding.

00:04:48.657 --> 00:04:51.490
Listen, i talked to my
producer, and it is looking good.

00:05:07.958 --> 00:05:09.857
Oh, man, that's so not cool.

00:05:09.891 --> 00:05:13.357
I just swept the telesca
house with the emf. It's clean.

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:16.024
And last night, while you were...

00:05:16.058 --> 00:05:17.290
Out...

00:05:17.324 --> 00:05:18.624
Oh, good times.

00:05:18.657 --> 00:05:20.290
...i checked the history of the house.

00:05:20.324 --> 00:05:21.924
No hauntings, no violent crimes,

00:05:21.958 --> 00:05:24.457
Nothing strange about the
telescas themselves, either.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.791
So if it's not the people
and it's not the house,

00:05:26.824 --> 00:05:28.390
Then maybe it's the contents -

00:05:28.424 --> 00:05:30.591
A cursed object or
something. House is clean.

00:05:30.624 --> 00:05:31.991
You said that.

00:05:32.024 --> 00:05:33.024
No, i mean it's empty.

00:05:33.058 --> 00:05:35.058
No furniture, nothing.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:37.390
Where's all their stuff?

00:06:05.424 --> 00:06:08.524
Silent auctions, estate sales -

00:06:08.557 --> 00:06:11.190
It's like a garage sale for
w.A.S.P.S, if you ask me.

00:06:11.223 --> 00:06:12.557
Can i help you, gentlemen?

00:06:15.223 --> 00:06:18.090
I'd like some champagne, please.

00:06:18.123 --> 00:06:19.857
He's not a waiter.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:26.424
I'm sam connors.

00:06:26.457 --> 00:06:29.058
This is my brother, dean.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:31.223
We are art dealers with connors limited.

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:33.190
You're art dealers? That's right.

00:06:33.223 --> 00:06:35.624
I'm daniel blake. This
is my auction house.

00:06:35.657 --> 00:06:38.824
Now, gentlemen, this
is a private showing,

00:06:38.857 --> 00:06:41.757
And i don't remember seeing
you on the guest list.

00:06:41.791 --> 00:06:43.090
We're there, chuckles.

00:06:43.123 --> 00:06:45.290
You just need to take another look.

00:06:45.324 --> 00:06:46.724
Oh, finally.

00:06:49.257 --> 00:06:50.524
Cheers.

00:07:08.591 --> 00:07:11.791
A fine example of american
primitive, wouldn't you say?

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:20.691
Well, i'd say it's more
grant wood than grandma moses

00:07:22.324 --> 00:07:23.757
But you knew that.

00:07:23.791 --> 00:07:25.424
You just wanted to see if i did.

00:07:25.457 --> 00:07:27.257
Guilty.

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:29.958
And clumsy. I apologize.

00:07:29.991 --> 00:07:31.924
I'm sarah blake.

00:07:31.958 --> 00:07:34.524
I'm sam.

00:07:34.557 --> 00:07:38.991
This is my...brother, dean.

00:07:39.024 --> 00:07:40.424
Dean. Hmm.

00:07:40.457 --> 00:07:42.090
Can we get you some more mini quiche?

00:07:42.123 --> 00:07:44.657
Mnh-Mnh, i'm good. Thanks.

00:07:44.691 --> 00:07:47.123
So, can i help you with something?

00:07:47.157 --> 00:07:49.490
Yeah, actually.

00:07:49.524 --> 00:07:52.357
What can you tell us
about the telesca estate?

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.557
The whole thing's pretty
grisly if you ask me,

00:07:54.591 --> 00:07:56.557
Selling their things this soon.

00:07:56.591 --> 00:07:58.691
But dad's right about one thing -

00:07:58.724 --> 00:08:00.958
Sensationalism brings out the crowds.

00:08:00.991 --> 00:08:03.424
Even the rich ones.

00:08:06.223 --> 00:08:08.290
Is it possible to see the provenances?

00:08:08.324 --> 00:08:12.123
I'm afraid there isn't
any chance of that.

00:08:12.157 --> 00:08:14.123
Why not?

00:08:14.157 --> 00:08:15.724
You're not on the guest list...

00:08:15.757 --> 00:08:17.290
And i think it's time to leave.

00:08:17.324 --> 00:08:19.324
Well, we don't have to be
told twice. Apparently, you do.

00:08:19.357 --> 00:08:20.390
Okay, it's all right.

00:08:20.424 --> 00:08:23.290
We don't want any trouble. We'll go.

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:32.457
Dad, that was rude.

00:08:35.357 --> 00:08:37.791
Grant wood, grandma moses
- What?

00:08:37.824 --> 00:08:39.157
Art history course.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:40.757
It's good for meeting girls.

00:08:40.791 --> 00:08:42.591
It's like i don't even know you.

00:08:59.591 --> 00:09:00.691
Huh.Huh.

00:09:00.724 --> 00:09:02.891
And what was the providence?

00:09:02.924 --> 00:09:04.024
Provenance.

00:09:04.058 --> 00:09:05.490
It's a certificate of origin,

00:09:05.524 --> 00:09:06.857
Like a biography, you know?

00:09:06.891 --> 00:09:09.123
We can use them to track
the history of the pieces,

00:09:09.157 --> 00:09:10.857
See if anything's got a freaky past.

00:09:10.891 --> 00:09:13.223
We're not getting
anything out of chuckles,

00:09:13.257 --> 00:09:14.691
But, uh, sarah... yeah.

00:09:14.724 --> 00:09:16.591
Maybe you can get her
to write it on a napkin.

00:09:16.624 --> 00:09:18.024
Not me.

00:09:18.058 --> 00:09:19.424
Oh, no, no, no, no.

00:09:19.457 --> 00:09:21.123
Pickups are your thing, dean.

00:09:21.157 --> 00:09:23.290
It wasn't my butt she was checking out.

00:09:23.324 --> 00:09:26.624
In other words, you want me
to use her to get information.

00:09:26.657 --> 00:09:28.190
Sometimes you got to
take one for the team.

00:09:28.223 --> 00:09:30.724
Call sarah.

00:09:35.058 --> 00:09:36.490
Nice place.

00:09:36.524 --> 00:09:37.624
Yeah.

00:09:45.991 --> 00:09:47.090
Glad you called.

00:09:48.157 --> 00:09:50.324
Surprised, but glad.

00:09:50.357 --> 00:09:51.390
Yeah?

00:09:51.424 --> 00:09:53.223
Although you seemed to have a hard time

00:09:53.257 --> 00:09:55.624
Getting out the words, "would
you like to have dinner?"

00:09:55.657 --> 00:09:57.724
Yeah.

00:09:57.757 --> 00:10:00.924
I haven't really been
on a date in a while.

00:10:00.958 --> 00:10:02.390
Welcome to the club.

00:10:02.424 --> 00:10:04.857
You're kidding me.

00:10:04.891 --> 00:10:08.657
Man: here we are.

00:10:08.691 --> 00:10:10.290
The wine list.

00:10:23.691 --> 00:10:28.424
I don't know about romeo
here, but i'll have a beer.

00:10:30.724 --> 00:10:31.757
And you?

00:10:31.791 --> 00:10:33.090
I will, too.

00:10:33.123 --> 00:10:34.157
Certainly.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.524
Sam: so, you studied art in school, huh?

00:10:36.557 --> 00:10:37.591
Sarah: it's true.

00:10:37.624 --> 00:10:38.691
I was an artist -

00:10:38.724 --> 00:10:42.657
A terrible, terrible artist.

00:10:42.691 --> 00:10:44.657
That's why i'm in the auction business.

00:10:44.691 --> 00:10:46.190
And you were pre-Law?

00:10:46.223 --> 00:10:47.290
Yeah.

00:10:47.324 --> 00:10:50.290
But you didn't go to
law school. How come?

00:10:50.324 --> 00:10:54.024
Uh, it's a really long
story for another time.

00:10:54.058 --> 00:10:56.657
You're not like any art
dealer i've ever met.

00:11:01.757 --> 00:11:04.058
So...what did you mean when you said

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:05.724
You hadn't been on a date in a while?

00:11:05.757 --> 00:11:07.490
Trying to make me feel
like i'm not such a loser?

00:11:07.524 --> 00:11:09.223
I'm sure many things, sam.

00:11:09.257 --> 00:11:12.390
I'm also sure "loser" isn't one of them.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:19.490
It was my mom.

00:11:19.524 --> 00:11:21.757
She died about a year ago.

00:11:21.791 --> 00:11:24.357
Totally unexpected.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:27.824
It really threw me.

00:11:29.524 --> 00:11:35.190
I went into this shell
- A nice, warm, safe shell.

00:11:35.223 --> 00:11:37.991
But lately, i've been thinking...

00:11:38.024 --> 00:11:41.624
It's not what she would
have wanted for me.

00:11:41.657 --> 00:11:43.123
So...

00:11:48.257 --> 00:11:49.557
So, what about you?

00:11:49.591 --> 00:11:52.290
You're a reasonably attractive guy.

00:11:53.958 --> 00:11:55.691
Reasonably.

00:11:55.724 --> 00:11:58.891
Why haven't you been out and about?

00:12:07.123 --> 00:12:10.824
Another long story for another time.

00:12:16.991 --> 00:12:18.857
So, she just handed the
providences over to you?

00:12:18.891 --> 00:12:20.058
Provenances.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.924
Provenances? Yes, we
went back to her place.

00:12:22.958 --> 00:12:25.257
I got a copy of the papers.

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:26.757
And?

00:12:26.791 --> 00:12:30.024
And nothing. That's it. I left.

00:12:30.058 --> 00:12:34.424
You didn't have to con her
or do any special favors?

00:12:34.457 --> 00:12:36.457
Would you get your mind
out of the gutter, please?

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:38.991
When this whole thing's done,
we could stick around a bit.

00:12:39.024 --> 00:12:40.757
Why? So you could take her out again.

00:12:40.791 --> 00:12:42.624
It's obvious you're into
her. Even i can see that.

00:12:42.657 --> 00:12:44.924
Hey, all right. I think
i got something here.

00:12:49.157 --> 00:12:50.958
"Portrait of isaiah merchant's family,

00:12:50.991 --> 00:12:52.324
Painted 1910."

00:12:52.357 --> 00:12:54.424
Now compare the names of the
owners with dad's journal.

00:12:58.724 --> 00:13:02.490
"First purchased in 1912 to peter sims."

00:13:02.524 --> 00:13:04.724
Peter sims murdered, 1912.

00:13:08.791 --> 00:13:11.424
Same thing in 1945.

00:13:11.457 --> 00:13:13.958
Oh, same thing in 1970.

00:13:13.991 --> 00:13:15.223
Then stored,

00:13:15.257 --> 00:13:17.591
Until it was donated to a
charity auction last month,

00:13:17.624 --> 00:13:19.490
Where the telescas bought it.

00:13:19.524 --> 00:13:22.190
So, what do you think?
It's haunted or cursed?

00:13:22.223 --> 00:13:24.390
Either way, it's toast.

00:13:46.757 --> 00:13:48.324
Go ahead.

00:14:33.058 --> 00:14:34.424
Ugly-Ass thing.

00:14:34.457 --> 00:14:37.324
If you ask me, we're doing
the art world a favor.

00:15:06.974 --> 00:15:09.240
We got a problem. I
can't find my wallet.

00:15:09.974 --> 00:15:11.741
How's that my problem?

00:15:11.774 --> 00:15:15.108
'Cause i think i dropped it
in the warehouse last night.

00:15:15.141 --> 00:15:16.141
You're kidding, right?

00:15:16.174 --> 00:15:17.874
I mean, it's got my prints, my i.D. -

00:15:17.907 --> 00:15:19.974
Well, my fake i.D.,
anyway, but we got to get it

00:15:20.007 --> 00:15:21.807
Before somebody else finds it. Come on.

00:15:32.074 --> 00:15:34.141
How do you lose your wallet, dean?

00:15:35.907 --> 00:15:37.741
Hey, guys.

00:15:37.774 --> 00:15:40.041
Sarah. Hey.

00:15:40.074 --> 00:15:41.640
What are you doing here?

00:15:41.674 --> 00:15:43.874
Oh...

00:15:43.907 --> 00:15:45.240
We're
- We're leaving town,

00:15:45.273 --> 00:15:47.373
And, you know, we came to say goodbye.

00:15:47.407 --> 00:15:49.208
What are you talking about, sam?

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:52.041
We're sticking around for
at least another day or two.

00:15:52.074 --> 00:15:53.607
Oh, sam, by the way,

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:57.041
I wanted to give you
that 20 bucks i owe you.

00:15:57.074 --> 00:16:00.373
I always forget.

00:16:00.407 --> 00:16:02.474
There you go.

00:16:05.174 --> 00:16:06.974
Well, i'll leave you
two crazy kids alone.

00:16:07.007 --> 00:16:09.607
I got to go do... something...somewhere.

00:16:16.841 --> 00:16:18.741
So...

00:16:18.774 --> 00:16:20.141
I had a good time last night.

00:16:20.174 --> 00:16:22.174
Yeah. Yeah, i did, too.

00:16:22.208 --> 00:16:25.174
Maybe we should do it again sometime?

00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:29.741
You know, i'd love to, i really would,

00:16:29.774 --> 00:16:31.574
But dean
- He was just screwing around.

00:16:31.607 --> 00:16:33.841
We really are taking off today.

00:16:33.874 --> 00:16:36.041
Oh. Oh.

00:16:36.074 --> 00:16:37.474
Now that's too bad.

00:16:37.507 --> 00:16:40.307
Oh, my god! What?

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:41.741
The -

00:16:41.774 --> 00:16:43.373
That painting...

00:16:43.407 --> 00:16:45.607
Looks so good.

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:48.941
If you can call that monstrosity good,

00:16:48.974 --> 00:16:50.707
Then, yeah, i guess.

00:16:50.741 --> 00:16:52.741
Sarah, what do you know
about that painting?

00:16:52.774 --> 00:16:54.974
Not much. Just that it creeps me out.

00:16:55.007 --> 00:16:56.440
We sold it to the telescas

00:16:56.474 --> 00:16:58.440
At a charity auction the
night they were murdered.

00:16:58.474 --> 00:17:00.974
And now you're just gonna sell it again?

00:17:01.007 --> 00:17:03.907
As much as my dad wants
to, no. I won't let him.

00:17:03.941 --> 00:17:05.874
I think it'd be in bad taste.

00:17:05.907 --> 00:17:07.674
Good, yeah. You know what? Don't. Don't.

00:17:07.707 --> 00:17:09.307
Make sure you don't, okay? Why?

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:11.407
Don't tell me you're interested in that.

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:13.273
No, god, no. Not in buying it, no.

00:17:13.307 --> 00:17:15.874
I got to go. I got to
take care of something.

00:17:15.907 --> 00:17:17.440
But, um, i will call you back.

00:17:17.474 --> 00:17:19.007
I will call you. I'll see you later.

00:17:19.041 --> 00:17:21.373
Wait, so you're not leaving tonight?

00:17:21.407 --> 00:17:24.874
No, i guess not. I'll see you.

00:17:26.874 --> 00:17:28.741
Okay.

00:17:30.841 --> 00:17:33.841
I don't understand, dean.
We burned the damn thing.

00:17:33.874 --> 00:17:35.941
Yeah, thank you, captain obvious.

00:17:35.974 --> 00:17:39.907
We just need to figure out
another way to get rid of it.

00:17:39.941 --> 00:17:41.041
Any ideas?

00:17:41.074 --> 00:17:42.307
Okay, all right.

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:44.807
Well, um, in almost all the
lore about haunted paintings,

00:17:44.841 --> 00:17:46.574
It's always the painting's
subject that haunts them.

00:17:46.607 --> 00:17:48.373
Yeah? All right.

00:17:48.407 --> 00:17:50.874
So we need to figure out
everything there is to know

00:17:50.907 --> 00:17:53.640
About that creepy-Ass family
in that creepy-Ass painting.

00:17:53.674 --> 00:17:55.774
What were their names again?

00:17:56.807 --> 00:17:58.108
The isaiah merchant family, right?

00:17:58.141 --> 00:17:59.907
Yeah, that's right.

00:17:59.941 --> 00:18:03.407
I dug up every scrap of
local history i could find.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:05.440
So, uh, are you boys crime buffs?

00:18:05.474 --> 00:18:08.407
Kind of. Why do you ask?

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:09.774
Well...

00:18:13.373 --> 00:18:15.307
Yes. Yeah, that sounds about right.

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:16.907
The whole family was killed?

00:18:16.941 --> 00:18:19.674
It seems this isaiah, he
slits his kids' throats,

00:18:19.707 --> 00:18:21.707
Then his wife, then himself.

00:18:21.741 --> 00:18:25.507
Now, he was a barber by
trade. Used a straight razor.

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:27.307
Why'd he do it?

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:29.607
Well, let's look.

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:31.640
Uh, "people who knew
him described isaiah

00:18:31.674 --> 00:18:33.607
"As having a stern
and harsh temperament,

00:18:33.640 --> 00:18:35.307
And controlled his
family with an iron fist."

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:40.108
Wife, two sons, adopted daughter
- Yeah, yeah.

00:18:40.141 --> 00:18:42.574
There were whispers that the
wife was gonna take the kids

00:18:42.607 --> 00:18:46.474
And leave, which, of course,
you know, in that day and age...

00:18:46.507 --> 00:18:49.607
So instead, old man isaiah,
well, he gave them all a shave.

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:50.607
Kkkch!

00:18:52.874 --> 00:18:54.807
Does it say what happened to the bodies?

00:18:54.841 --> 00:18:56.307
They were all cremated.

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:01.041
Anything else? Yeah.

00:19:01.074 --> 00:19:03.974
Actually, i found a
picture of the family.

00:19:04.007 --> 00:19:05.774
It's right here somewhere.

00:19:05.807 --> 00:19:07.707
Right. Here it is.

00:19:15.807 --> 00:19:18.440
Hey, could we get a
copy of this, please?

00:19:18.474 --> 00:19:20.307
Sure.

00:19:24.407 --> 00:19:25.607
Dad...

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:28.807
You promised you wouldn't
sell that painting.

00:19:28.841 --> 00:19:30.674
I know, sweetie, but evelyn's offered

00:19:30.707 --> 00:19:32.208
A persuasive amount of money.

00:19:32.240 --> 00:19:35.774
You're shameless, you know that?

00:19:35.807 --> 00:19:38.574
For that kind of money,
i can afford to be.

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.240
Sam: i'm telling you,
man. I'm sure of it.

00:19:45.273 --> 00:19:47.774
The painting at the auction
house, dad is looking down.

00:19:47.807 --> 00:19:49.607
The painting here, dad's looking out.

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:50.974
The painting has changed, dean.

00:19:51.007 --> 00:19:53.307
So you think that daddy dearest
is trapped in the painting,

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:54.974
And he's handing out columbian neckties

00:19:55.007 --> 00:19:57.540
Like he did with his family?
Well, yeah, it seems like it.

00:19:57.574 --> 00:19:59.574
But if his bones are already dusted,

00:19:59.607 --> 00:20:01.407
Then how are we gonna stop him?

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:02.774
Well, if isaiah's position changed,

00:20:02.807 --> 00:20:04.874
Then maybe some other things in
the painting changed, as well.

00:20:04.907 --> 00:20:06.273
It could give us some clues.

00:20:06.307 --> 00:20:07.574
Like a "da vinci code" deal?

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:09.674
I don't know.

00:20:09.707 --> 00:20:12.273
I'm still waiting for
the movie on that one.

00:20:12.307 --> 00:20:14.373
Anyway, we got to get back
in and see that painting,

00:20:14.407 --> 00:20:16.440
Which is a good thing,
because you can get more time

00:20:16.474 --> 00:20:17.707
To crush on your girlfriend.

00:20:17.741 --> 00:20:19.974
Dude...enough already.

00:20:20.007 --> 00:20:22.007
What? "What?" Ever since we got here,

00:20:22.041 --> 00:20:24.108
You've been trying to
pimp me out to sarah.

00:20:24.141 --> 00:20:25.340
Just back off, all right?

00:20:25.373 --> 00:20:26.741
Well, you like her, don't you?

00:20:26.774 --> 00:20:28.440
All right, you like her. She likes you.

00:20:28.474 --> 00:20:30.007
You're both consenting adults.

00:20:30.041 --> 00:20:31.108
What's the point, dean?

00:20:31.141 --> 00:20:32.607
We'll just leave. We always leave.

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:34.373
Well, i'm not talking
about marriage, sam.

00:20:34.407 --> 00:20:36.307
I don't get it. What do
you care if i hook up?

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:38.208
Maybe you wouldn't be
so cranky all the time.

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:46.340
Seriously, sam, this isn't
about just hooking up, okay?

00:20:46.373 --> 00:20:49.340
I think that this sarah
girl could be good for you.

00:20:51.741 --> 00:20:55.108
And i don't mean any
disrespect, but i'm -

00:20:55.141 --> 00:20:57.074
I'm sure that this is
about jessica, right?

00:20:58.074 --> 00:21:02.874
Now, i don't know what it's like
to lose somebody like that...

00:21:02.907 --> 00:21:04.774
But...

00:21:04.807 --> 00:21:06.807
I would think that she
would want you to be happy.

00:21:09.108 --> 00:21:12.141
God forbid, have fun once in a while.

00:21:12.174 --> 00:21:13.373
Wouldn't she?

00:21:18.041 --> 00:21:19.807
Yeah, i know she would.

00:21:24.807 --> 00:21:30.240
Yeah, you're right. Part
of this is about jessica.

00:21:30.273 --> 00:21:31.640
But not the main part.

00:21:31.674 --> 00:21:33.574
What's it about?

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:39.707
Yeah, all right.

00:21:39.741 --> 00:21:42.707
Well, we still got to see that painting,

00:21:42.741 --> 00:21:46.108
Which means you still
got to call sarah, so...

00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:00.074
Sarah, hey. It's sam.

00:22:00.108 --> 00:22:01.941
Hey, hi.

00:22:01.974 --> 00:22:04.208
Good, good, yeah. What about you?

00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:06.974
Yeah, good. Good, really good. Smooth.

00:22:07.007 --> 00:22:09.507
So, uh
- So, listen.

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:11.340
Me and my brother were thinking

00:22:11.373 --> 00:22:13.440
That maybe we'd like to come back in

00:22:13.474 --> 00:22:15.273
And look at the painting again.

00:22:15.307 --> 00:22:17.974
I think maybe we are
interested in buying it.

00:22:18.007 --> 00:22:19.174
Wait, what?

00:22:19.208 --> 00:22:22.307
Who'd you sell it to?

00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:24.841
Sarah, i need an address right now.

00:23:09.974 --> 00:23:11.108
Sam, what's happening?

00:23:11.140 --> 00:23:13.240
I told you you shouldn't have come.

00:23:16.774 --> 00:23:18.008
Hello, anybody home?!

00:23:18.041 --> 00:23:20.574
You said evelyn might be in
danger. What kind of danger?

00:23:20.607 --> 00:23:24.474
I can't knock this sucker
down. I got to pick it.

00:23:24.507 --> 00:23:27.041
What are you guys, burglars?

00:23:27.074 --> 00:23:28.374
I wish it was that simple.

00:23:28.407 --> 00:23:30.841
Look, you really should wait in the car.

00:23:30.874 --> 00:23:32.240
Ugh.

00:23:32.273 --> 00:23:33.741
The hell i will. Evelyn's a friend.

00:23:33.774 --> 00:23:34.807
Evelyn?

00:23:34.841 --> 00:23:36.407
Sam: evelyn!

00:23:41.307 --> 00:23:42.540
Evelyn?

00:23:53.074 --> 00:23:55.741
Evelyn?

00:23:55.774 --> 00:23:57.140
It's sarah blake.

00:23:57.173 --> 00:23:58.607
Are you all right?

00:23:58.641 --> 00:23:59.907
Sarah, don't! Sarah!

00:24:06.008 --> 00:24:08.707
Oh, my god! Oh, my god!

00:24:18.108 --> 00:24:20.874
Hey. You all right?

00:24:20.907 --> 00:24:22.307
No, actually.

00:24:22.340 --> 00:24:25.641
I just lied to the cops and told
them i went to evelyn's alone

00:24:25.674 --> 00:24:28.108
And found her like that.

00:24:28.140 --> 00:24:29.273
Thank you. Don't thank me.

00:24:29.307 --> 00:24:30.674
I'm about to call them right back

00:24:30.707 --> 00:24:32.540
If you don't tell me
what the hell is going on.

00:24:32.574 --> 00:24:34.041
Who's killing these people?

00:24:38.173 --> 00:24:39.741
"What."

00:24:39.774 --> 00:24:41.207
What?

00:24:41.240 --> 00:24:42.474
It's not "who."

00:24:42.507 --> 00:24:45.407
It's "what" is killing those people.

00:24:48.340 --> 00:24:50.907
Sarah, you saw that painting move.

00:24:50.941 --> 00:24:53.741
No.

00:24:53.774 --> 00:24:56.440
No, i was
- I was seeing things.

00:24:56.474 --> 00:24:57.807
It's impossible.

00:24:57.841 --> 00:24:59.507
Yeah, well, welcome to our world.

00:24:59.540 --> 00:25:02.774
Sarah, i know this sounds crazy...

00:25:02.807 --> 00:25:05.041
But we think that that
painting is haunted.

00:25:09.440 --> 00:25:10.941
You're joking.

00:25:15.240 --> 00:25:17.741
You're not joking.

00:25:17.774 --> 00:25:20.207
God, the guys i go out with.

00:25:20.240 --> 00:25:21.874
Sarah, think about it.

00:25:21.907 --> 00:25:25.574
Evelyn, the telescas
- They both had the painting.

00:25:25.607 --> 00:25:27.207
And there have been others before that.

00:25:27.240 --> 00:25:28.774
Wherever this thing goes, people die,

00:25:28.807 --> 00:25:31.173
And we're just trying to stop it...

00:25:31.207 --> 00:25:32.607
And that's the truth.

00:25:32.641 --> 00:25:37.507
Well, then, i guess you better show me.

00:25:37.540 --> 00:25:38.540
I'm coming with you.

00:25:38.574 --> 00:25:39.941
What? No.

00:25:39.974 --> 00:25:42.407
Sarah, no. You should just go home.

00:25:42.440 --> 00:25:45.108
This stuff can get dangerous, and

00:25:47.008 --> 00:25:49.008
And i don't want you to get hurt.

00:25:49.041 --> 00:25:50.907
Look, you guys are probably crazy,

00:25:50.941 --> 00:25:52.474
But if you're right about this,

00:25:52.507 --> 00:25:54.507
When me and my dad sold that painting,

00:25:54.540 --> 00:25:56.540
We might have got these people killed.

00:25:56.574 --> 00:25:59.540
I'm not saying i'm not scared,
'cause i am scared as hell,

00:25:59.574 --> 00:26:01.741
But i'm not gonna run and hide, either.

00:26:04.607 --> 00:26:06.474
So are we going or what?

00:26:06.507 --> 00:26:07.674
Sam

00:26:09.707 --> 00:26:11.041
Marry that girl.

00:26:14.041 --> 00:26:17.874
Uh... isn't this a crime scene?

00:26:17.907 --> 00:26:20.474
You've already lied to the
cops. What's another infraction?

00:26:39.607 --> 00:26:43.207
Aren't you worried that it's
gonna, you know, kill us?

00:26:43.240 --> 00:26:45.407
No, it seems to do its thing at night.

00:26:45.440 --> 00:26:46.874
I think we're all right in daylight.

00:26:51.907 --> 00:26:54.140
Sam, check it out.

00:26:54.173 --> 00:26:55.607
The razor
- It's closed in this one,

00:26:55.641 --> 00:26:57.607
But it's open in that one.
What are you guys looking for?

00:26:57.641 --> 00:26:59.374
If the spirit's changing
aspects of the painting,

00:26:59.407 --> 00:27:02.140
Maybe it's doing so for a reason.

00:27:02.173 --> 00:27:06.374
Hey, hey, look at this
- The painting in the painting.

00:27:11.108 --> 00:27:13.774
It looks like a crypt or
a mausoleum or something.

00:27:24.574 --> 00:27:25.807
"Merchant."

00:27:34.540 --> 00:27:37.207
This is the third
boneyard we've checked.

00:27:37.240 --> 00:27:40.474
This ghost is jerking us around.

00:27:40.507 --> 00:27:43.440
So, this is what you
guys do for a living?

00:27:43.474 --> 00:27:46.008
Not exactly.

00:27:46.041 --> 00:27:48.474
We don't get paid.

00:27:48.507 --> 00:27:51.074
Well, mazel tov.

00:27:52.674 --> 00:27:54.807
Over there.

00:28:29.707 --> 00:28:33.874
Okay, that right there is the
creepiest thing i've ever seen.

00:28:33.907 --> 00:28:36.741
It was sort of a tradition at the time.

00:28:36.774 --> 00:28:37.974
Whenever a child died,

00:28:38.008 --> 00:28:40.240
Sometimes they'd preserve
the kid's favorite toy

00:28:40.273 --> 00:28:43.074
In a glass case, put it next
to the headstone in the crypt.

00:28:48.707 --> 00:28:50.474
Notice anything strange here?

00:28:50.507 --> 00:28:51.974
Uh, where do i start?

00:28:52.008 --> 00:28:53.540
No, that's not what i mean.

00:28:53.574 --> 00:28:54.641
Look at the urns.

00:28:56.907 --> 00:28:58.841
Yeah, there are only four.

00:28:58.874 --> 00:29:01.074
Mom and the three kids.

00:29:01.108 --> 00:29:02.807
Daddy dearest isn't here.

00:29:05.074 --> 00:29:06.574
So where is he?

00:29:06.607 --> 00:29:09.207
Sarah: so, what exactly is
your brother doing in there?

00:29:09.240 --> 00:29:11.074
Searching county death certificates,

00:29:11.108 --> 00:29:13.674
Trying to find out what
happened to isaiah's body.

00:29:13.707 --> 00:29:15.307
How'd he even get in the door?

00:29:15.340 --> 00:29:19.741
Lying and subterfuge, mostly.

00:29:21.941 --> 00:29:25.240
You have a, um
- You have an eyelash on your...

00:29:25.273 --> 00:29:27.074
You have it right
- No. Uh, you know what?

00:29:29.140 --> 00:29:30.440
Do you mind if i -

00:29:30.474 --> 00:29:32.841
No. Okay.

00:29:32.874 --> 00:29:34.841
Okay, i got it.

00:29:34.874 --> 00:29:35.941
Make a wish.

00:29:44.173 --> 00:29:45.574
Sam, can i ask you something?

00:29:45.607 --> 00:29:48.240
Yeah, sure. I don't mean to be forward,

00:29:48.273 --> 00:29:52.941
But a girl could wait here forever.

00:29:52.974 --> 00:29:56.974
Is there something here
between us, or am i delusional?

00:29:57.008 --> 00:29:59.041
You're not delusional.

00:29:59.074 --> 00:30:02.140
But there's a "but" coming.

00:30:02.173 --> 00:30:05.240
But...

00:30:05.273 --> 00:30:07.841
I don't think this would be a good idea.

00:30:09.907 --> 00:30:11.041
Can i ask why?

00:30:13.108 --> 00:30:14.273
'Cause i like you.

00:30:16.674 --> 00:30:18.674
Wait. You lost me.

00:30:21.074 --> 00:30:23.807
Look, it's hard to explain.

00:30:23.841 --> 00:30:28.307
It's just that when
people are around me...

00:30:28.340 --> 00:30:30.074
I don't know, they get hurt.

00:30:30.108 --> 00:30:31.140
What do you mean?

00:30:31.173 --> 00:30:34.407
I mean, like, physically hurt.

00:30:34.440 --> 00:30:37.474
With what my brother and i do, it's...

00:30:42.941 --> 00:30:46.240
Sarah...

00:30:46.273 --> 00:30:48.240
I had a girlfriend.

00:30:49.641 --> 00:30:52.041
And she died.

00:30:52.074 --> 00:30:55.807
And my mom died, too.

00:30:55.841 --> 00:30:59.841
I don't know, it's like...

00:30:59.874 --> 00:31:03.074
It's like i'm cursed or something...

00:31:03.108 --> 00:31:04.707
Like death just follows me around.

00:31:04.741 --> 00:31:07.273
Look, i'm not scared of much,

00:31:07.307 --> 00:31:09.774
But if i let myself have
feelings for anybody -

00:31:09.807 --> 00:31:11.674
You're scared they get hurt, too.

00:31:13.574 --> 00:31:18.474
That's very sweet and very archaic.

00:31:18.507 --> 00:31:20.008
Sorry? Look, i'm a big girl, sam.

00:31:20.041 --> 00:31:22.474
It's not your job to
make decisions for me.

00:31:22.507 --> 00:31:24.807
There's always a chance of getting hurt.

00:31:24.841 --> 00:31:26.540
I'm not talking about a broken heart

00:31:26.574 --> 00:31:27.707
And a tub of haagen-Dazs.

00:31:27.741 --> 00:31:28.907
I'm talking about life and death.

00:31:28.941 --> 00:31:30.974
And tomorrow, i could get hit by a bus.

00:31:31.008 --> 00:31:32.108
That's what life is.

00:31:33.173 --> 00:31:36.540
Look, i know losing somebody you love
- It's terrible.

00:31:36.574 --> 00:31:41.108
You shut yourself off.
Believe me, i know.

00:31:41.140 --> 00:31:43.807
But when you shut out pain...

00:31:43.841 --> 00:31:46.041
You shut out everything else, too.

00:31:46.074 --> 00:31:49.641
Sarah, you don't understand.
The pain that i went through...

00:31:49.674 --> 00:31:54.207
I can't go through it again. I can't.

00:31:58.240 --> 00:31:59.874
Am i interrupting something?

00:31:59.907 --> 00:32:01.707
No. Not at all.

00:32:01.741 --> 00:32:03.108
Apparently.

00:32:03.140 --> 00:32:04.941
So, what'd you get? Pay dirt.

00:32:04.974 --> 00:32:08.374
Apparently, the surviving
relatives of the merchant family

00:32:08.407 --> 00:32:10.907
Were so ashamed of isaiah that
they didn't want him interred

00:32:10.941 --> 00:32:13.273
With the family, so they
handed him over to the county.

00:32:13.307 --> 00:32:15.374
The county gave him a pauper's funeral,

00:32:15.407 --> 00:32:16.807
Economy-Style.

00:32:16.841 --> 00:32:19.074
Turns out he wasn't cremated.
He was buried in a pine box.

00:32:19.108 --> 00:32:20.540
<i>So there are bones to burn.</i>

00:32:20.574 --> 00:32:22.974
There are bones to burn.
Tell me you know where.

00:32:36.641 --> 00:32:38.574
You guys seem to be

00:32:38.607 --> 00:32:40.707
Uncomfortably comfortable with this.

00:32:40.741 --> 00:32:45.240
Well...this isn't exactly
the first grave we dug.

00:32:45.273 --> 00:32:49.574
Still think i'm a catch?

00:32:51.008 --> 00:32:53.074
Think i got something.

00:33:19.140 --> 00:33:20.974
Dean: you been a real
pain in the ass, isaiah.

00:33:23.008 --> 00:33:24.641
Good riddance.

00:33:36.140 --> 00:33:37.874
Dean, keep the motor running.

00:33:37.907 --> 00:33:40.707
I thought the painting was harmless now.

00:33:40.741 --> 00:33:43.507
Better safe than sorry.
We're gonna bury the sucker.

00:33:43.540 --> 00:33:44.641
I want to come with you.

00:33:44.674 --> 00:33:46.273
Are you sure?

00:33:46.307 --> 00:33:48.008
Hey, hey, hey.

00:33:48.041 --> 00:33:50.607
I'll stay here. You go make your move.

00:33:50.641 --> 00:33:52.474
S- S-Sam,
i'm serious!

00:34:19.874 --> 00:34:22.173
Uh, sam...

00:34:22.207 --> 00:34:24.941
You're the expert on
all this ghost stuff.

00:34:24.974 --> 00:34:26.374
Is that painting supposed
to look like that?

00:34:28.907 --> 00:34:31.008
Where's the little girl?

00:34:33.540 --> 00:34:34.974
And the razor?

00:34:49.941 --> 00:34:52.641
Dean! Hey, is that you?!

00:34:52.674 --> 00:34:54.140
Dean: sammy, you all right?!

00:34:59.340 --> 00:35:00.941
Tell me you slammed the front door.

00:35:00.974 --> 00:35:02.674
No, it wasn't me. I think
it was the little girl.

00:35:02.707 --> 00:35:04.774
Girl? What girl? Yeah,
she's out of the painting.

00:35:04.807 --> 00:35:06.307
I think it might have
been her all along.

00:35:06.340 --> 00:35:07.674
Wasn't the dad looking down at her?

00:35:07.707 --> 00:35:09.140
Maybe he was trying to warn us.

00:35:09.173 --> 00:35:11.574
Hey, let's recap later.
Just get us out of here.

00:35:11.607 --> 00:35:14.407
I'm trying to pick the lock, and
the door won't budge. Break it down.

00:35:14.440 --> 00:35:17.407
Okay, genius, let me grab my battering
ram! Dean, the damn thing's coming!

00:35:17.440 --> 00:35:19.574
You're gonna have to hold it
off until i figure something out.

00:35:19.607 --> 00:35:21.574
Get some salt or iron.

00:35:24.707 --> 00:35:26.907
What kind of house doesn't have salt?

00:35:26.941 --> 00:35:29.407
Hey, you find any
iron? No, what's it for?

00:35:29.440 --> 00:35:31.307
Iron repels evil spirits,
but it's got to be pure.

00:35:31.340 --> 00:35:33.574
Hurry.

00:35:33.607 --> 00:35:37.173
Uh, dean, give me a
sec. Don't go anywhere.

00:35:37.207 --> 00:35:39.707
Look at a chair. Sometimes the seats...

00:35:58.574 --> 00:35:59.674
Sam!

00:36:17.574 --> 00:36:19.874
That is just so wrong.

00:36:41.273 --> 00:36:44.108
Iron?

00:36:44.140 --> 00:36:45.173
Yeah.

00:36:45.207 --> 00:36:47.540
Sam, are you okay?

00:36:47.574 --> 00:36:48.574
Yeah, for now.

00:36:48.607 --> 00:36:49.974
How we gonna waste her?

00:36:50.008 --> 00:36:51.774
I don't know. She was already cremated.

00:36:51.807 --> 00:36:54.041
There's nothing left to burn.
Well, then, how's she still around?

00:36:54.074 --> 00:36:55.440
There must be something else.

00:36:56.741 --> 00:36:58.240
Sam, wait.

00:36:58.273 --> 00:37:00.440
We used to handle antique
dolls at the auction.

00:37:00.474 --> 00:37:03.540
Well, that's fascinating,
sarah, but important right now?

00:37:03.574 --> 00:37:06.707
Back then, they used to make
the dolls in the kid's image.

00:37:06.741 --> 00:37:07.941
I mean, everything.

00:37:07.974 --> 00:37:10.407
Like, they would use
the kid's real hair.

00:37:10.440 --> 00:37:11.607
Dean?

00:37:11.641 --> 00:37:14.574
Sarah says the doll might
have the girl's hair.

00:37:14.607 --> 00:37:17.574
Human remains
- Same as bones.

00:37:17.607 --> 00:37:19.440
Both: the mausoleum.

00:37:48.207 --> 00:37:49.974
Sam!

00:38:14.974 --> 00:38:15.974
Come on, dean.

00:38:36.207 --> 00:38:38.140
Come on! Come on!

00:39:30.240 --> 00:39:31.474
Sam, you good?

00:39:35.607 --> 00:39:36.674
Not bad.

00:39:55.524 --> 00:39:57.958
This was archived in the county records.

00:39:57.991 --> 00:40:00.524
The merchant's adopted
daughter, melanie.

00:40:00.557 --> 00:40:02.123
Know why she was up for adoption?

00:40:02.157 --> 00:40:05.024
'Cause her real family
was murdered in their beds.

00:40:05.058 --> 00:40:06.290
She killed them?

00:40:06.324 --> 00:40:08.058
Yeah, who would suspect
her? A sweet little girl.

00:40:08.090 --> 00:40:10.290
So then she kills isaiah and his family.

00:40:10.324 --> 00:40:11.791
The old man takes the blame.

00:40:11.824 --> 00:40:14.024
His spirit's been trying
to warn people ever since.

00:40:14.058 --> 00:40:15.724
Where's this one go?

00:40:15.757 --> 00:40:17.357
Take it out back and burn it.

00:40:19.290 --> 00:40:22.757
I'm serious, guys. Thanks.

00:40:25.490 --> 00:40:27.624
So, why'd the girl do it?

00:40:27.657 --> 00:40:29.624
Killing others, killing herself -

00:40:29.657 --> 00:40:31.691
Some people are just born tortured.

00:40:31.724 --> 00:40:34.390
So when they die, their
spirits are just as dark.

00:40:34.424 --> 00:40:36.657
Maybe. I don't really care. It's over.

00:40:36.691 --> 00:40:39.324
We move on.

00:40:41.157 --> 00:40:42.757
I guess this means you're leaving.

00:40:49.524 --> 00:40:53.457
I'll go wait in the car. See you, sarah.

00:40:57.757 --> 00:40:59.924
I'm the one who burned the
doll and destroyed the spirit,

00:40:59.958 --> 00:41:01.157
But don't thank me or anything.

00:41:07.190 --> 00:41:10.524
There are a million things
that i want to say to you,

00:41:10.557 --> 00:41:13.457
But for the life of me,
i can't think of one.

00:41:13.490 --> 00:41:16.390
Yeah, i'll miss you, too.

00:41:16.424 --> 00:41:18.924
You know, there's a
lesson in all of this.

00:41:18.958 --> 00:41:19.958
What's that?

00:41:19.991 --> 00:41:22.591
We all got through this in one piece.

00:41:23.691 --> 00:41:25.290
I didn't get hurt.

00:41:25.324 --> 00:41:27.324
Yeah, i'm glad for that.

00:41:27.357 --> 00:41:30.724
So maybe you're not cursed.

00:41:30.757 --> 00:41:33.223
Maybe...

00:41:36.557 --> 00:41:39.024
Maybe you'll come back and see me.

00:41:42.691 --> 00:41:44.257
I will.

00:42:28.058 --> 00:42:30.691
That's my boy.



00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
